@allenporter, is there any way I can 'ping' to see if the service is alive so that I can write a cron job that regularly checks if the service is connected and restarts it if not?
(Currently, I can test manually by trying to change the temperature either on my Nest phone app or in Homeassistant to check if the change is reflected in the other interface -- if not then, I need to reboot)

I ask because I am trying to track hvac usage which of course gets really messed up if the Nest integration fails, so I would like to automate a way to test if it is alive and reboot as necessary.

@allenporter is there any way to determine when the new version of the integration gets integrated in production HA release?
I wasn't able to find a version number on the HA Nest Integration page... and I would like to know when the new code is available so I can test it and confirm the fix works.
Thanks!
